{"cache_key uses hash(tuple(...)) which is non-deterministic across Python processes due to PYTHONHASHSEED randomization, reducing cache effectiveness and making invalidate_upsampling_cache unpredictable": 0.9700883626937866, "In error_upsampling.is_errors_query_for_error_upsampled_projects, accessing snuba_params.project_ids may raise AttributeError since SnubaParams may use 'projects' attribute instead": 0.26309967041015625, "_are_all_projects_error_upsampled takes project_ids: Sequence[int] but callers may pass Project model instances instead of ints, causing type mismatch when comparing against allowlist": 0.11545905470848083, "organization_events_stats has duplicated import blocks and a stray closing parenthesis that will cause a SyntaxError": 0.05200382322072983, "Cache key should include dataset name if eligibility is dataset dependent, or document why it doesn't": 0.3575587570667267, "transform_query_columns_for_error_upsampling returns 'upsampled_count() as count' but downstream consumers may expect different alias formats": 0.00883952621370554, "Possible code duplication in discover.function_converter around the toInt64/sum sample_weight block when inserting the new upsampled_count function": 0.05011022090911865, "invalidate_upsampling_cache is defined but never called when options change - need to wire an options change hook or document that it must be called manually": 0.6487035155296326, "Integration tests rely on specific sample_weight behavior mapping sample_rate to sample_weight in Snuba, making tests brittle": 0.11347004026174545, "Docstrings mention 'ALL projects are allowlisted and we're querying error events' but should also mention the dataset-dependent _should_apply_sample_weight_transform condition": 0.03886769339442253, "Missing explicit unit tests for caching behavior to ensure cache key stability": 0.8665096759796143}